      "baseRefName": "codex/research-online-ch2-unbounded-osd",
      "body": "Implements the strict-past FTL argmin rule from Orabona v10, Chapter 2 as a shared classical partial selector. Nine proofs establish feasible initialization, correctness of attained minima, exact nonattainment and causal prefix invariance. Eight concrete canaries cover trajectories, ties, empty sets, changed future losses and recovery queries. The package also reconciles existing Chapter 2 provenance and prescient dependencies.\n\nValidation: combined Lean root and Tests passed; the full harness passed 472 tests with 7 skips. Public statement and axiom audits, frozen-statement checks and two nonempty contributor gates passed. The clean local site at source commit `224bbe791966084d8abcaaf91695f9f3597ed5aa` preserves all 11,041 previous registry nodes and adds 13 production nodes. All 28 current desktop screenshots receive root and distinct staged automated review. Source contracts and receipts: `docs/contracts/online-ch2-reconciliation-v1` and `runs/online-ch2-reconciliation-20261010`.\n\nThis is one algorithm-definition foundation, with four definitions and nine proofs. It gives no new FTL regret guarantee or unconditional, executable or measurable optimizer. If P1 is `none`, there is no playable action; P2 = `some 0` is an independent longer-prefix query, not a valid interaction continuing after failure. All eight forward containers remain required and open, including six future mathematical claims awaiting enumeration. Chapter 2 remains partial; the whole-book Goal remains active.\n\nStacked on OPEN, unmerged draft PR #214 at exact head `2e06e21d2acb0bf41142b19266d66d89364e17a0`. The local site belongs to its source commit, not the later evidence head. No merge or deployment is included.\n",
